.TH SDE-GALLERY 1 "October 2026" "SDE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sde-gallery \- Gallery, the SDE photo library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sde-gallery
[\-\-select FILE] [\-\-slideshow FILE] [\-\-import] [\fIFOLDER\fR]
.br
.B sde-gallery
\-\-version | \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
Gallery organizes your photos: it browses them by date, folder, album and
device, keeps favorites and the albums you make, searches, imports from
cameras and memory cards, plays slideshows and works on many photos at
once. It does not edit single photos: opening a photo starts Photo
.RB ( sde-view (1)),
the image viewer and editor, and Gallery's quick preview has an
.B Edit in Photo
button.
.PP
Gallery shows the pictures in your XDG Pictures folder (see
.BR xdg-user-dir (1))
and in folders you add, grouped by month of their modification time.
The sidebar offers All Photos, Favorites, Recent (the last 30 days),
Screenshots (the Screenshots folder inside Pictures), the folder list,
your
.B Albums
and, under
.BR Devices ,
the cameras, SD cards, USB drives and other removable media mounted below
.I /media
or
.IR /run/media .
The device list follows
.I /proc/self/mountinfo
and changes as media are connected and removed.
A device can be browsed in place, imported, or ejected (the button shown
when the pointer is over it, or its context menu).
JPEG, PNG, GIF, BMP and SVG files are shown; WebP, TIFF, AVIF, HEIF and
JPEG XL are shown when the matching gdk-pixbuf loaders are installed.
Photos are shown upright following their EXIF orientation.
.PP
Thumbnails are made in the background and shared with other applications
through the freedesktop.org thumbnail cache in
.IR ~/.cache/thumbnails/normal
and
.IR ~/.cache/thumbnails/large .
.SS Albums
.B New Album
(Ctrl+N, or the sidebar) makes an album; photos are added with
.B Add to Album
(Ctrl+L, the selection bar or the photo menu) and removed with
.BR "Remove from Album" .
An album only lists photos: removing a photo from an album, or deleting an
album, never deletes files. Albums follow photos that are moved with
.B Move to Folder
and forget photos moved to the Trash. Right-click an album in the sidebar
to play a slideshow, rename or delete it.
.SS Working with many photos
Select photos with Ctrl+click, Shift+click or Ctrl+A. The selection bar
offers Favorite, Add to Album, More and Move to Trash; the photo menu
(right click, or More) also has:
.TP
.B Slideshow
of the selected photos (or of the whole view, F5).
.TP
.B Rotate Left, Rotate Right
JPEG photos are turned without loss of quality by changing their EXIF
orientation; PNG, WebP and TIFF are encoded again.
.TP
.B Resize and Export
Writes copies to a folder, at the original size or with the longest side
at 3840, 2048, 1280 or 640 pixels. JPEG copies keep the camera details;
GIF and SVG are exported as PNG. Existing files are never overwritten: the
copies get a number, as in
.IR "IMG_0001 (2).jpg" .
.TP
.B Copy to Folder, Move to Folder
Moving keeps favorites and albums up to date.
.TP
.B Share by Email
Opens a new message with the photos attached
.RB ( xdg-email (1)).
.SS Menus
.TP
.B File
Open File (opens it in Photo), Open Folder (browse any folder without
adding it), Import from Device, Add Folder to Library, New Album,
Refresh, Quit.
.TP
.B Edit
Select All, Select None, Add to Favorites, Add to Album, Remove from
Album, Rotate Left/Right, Resize and Export, Copy to Folder, Move to
Folder, Share by Email, Copy Path, Move to Trash, Edit in Photo, Quick
Preview, Set as Wallpaper, Show in Files.
.TP
.B View
Sort order, thumbnail size, Show Sidebar, Open Photos in Photo,
Slideshow, Full Screen.
.TP
.B Help
Keyboard Shortcuts, About Gallery.
.SS Import
Import from Device copies the photos of a device (or the selected ones)
to
.IR ~/Pictures/Imported/YYYY-MM-DD/ ,
the date being the day each photo was taken by the camera (its
modification time). Photos imported before (same name and size) are
skipped; other name clashes get a number, as in
.IR "DSC_0001 (2).JPG" .
Gallery is the default application for camera media
.RB ( x-content/image-dcf ),
so a file manager can offer it when a card is inserted.
.SS Photo
Double-click a photo or press Enter to open it in Photo (with
.B View > Open Photos in Photo
unset, or without Photo installed, in the quick preview instead; Ctrl+P
always opens the preview, Ctrl+E always opens Photo). Gallery starts Photo
with
.BI \-\-album= ID
and the current sort order, so that Photo steps through the same photos in
the same order (search results and albums are passed as lists). Edits,
deletions and new files made in Photo appear in Gallery at once; Photo's
.B Show in Gallery
selects the photo in the running Gallery, and Photo's slideshow (F5) plays
in Gallery.
.PP
Files are never deleted permanently: Move to Trash uses the
freedesktop.org Trash through GIO.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Arrows, Page Up/Down, Home, End
Move between photos. Shift extends the selection.
.TP
.B Ctrl+click, Shift+click, Space, Ctrl+A, Esc
Select photos, select all, clear the selection.
.TP
.B Enter, Ctrl+E, Ctrl+P
Open the photo in Photo, edit in Photo, quick preview.
.TP
.B + \- , Ctrl+mouse wheel
Change the thumbnail size (zoom in the preview).
.TP
.B Ctrl+F, Ctrl+O, Ctrl+Shift+O, Ctrl+I, Ctrl+R
Search, open a photo, open a folder, import from a device, reload.
.TP
.B Ctrl+D, Ctrl+L, Ctrl+N, Ctrl+C, Delete
Toggle favorite, add to an album, new album, copy paths, move to the
Trash.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+L, Ctrl+Shift+R, Ctrl+Shift+E, F5
Rotate left, rotate right, resize and export, slideshow.
.TP
.B F1, F9, F11, Ctrl+Q
Keyboard shortcuts, sidebar, full screen, quit.
.TP
.B Preview: 0, 1, I, F5, F11, Ctrl+E, Esc
Fit, actual size, details, slideshow, full screen, edit in Photo, back.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I FOLDER
Show the photos of
.I FOLDER
(a file: its folder, with the file selected).
.TP
.BI \-\-select " FILE"
Show and select
.IR FILE .
When Gallery is already running, the running window does it and is
raised; only one Gallery runs per display.
.TP
.BI \-\-slideshow " FILE"
Play a slideshow of the folder (or library view) of
.IR FILE ,
starting with it.
.TP
.B \-\-import
Import photos from a connected camera or card.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short usage summary.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sde/sde.conf
Section
.B [gallery]
keeps
.BR folders= ,
.BR favorites=
(lists separated by semicolons),
.BR thumbnail_size= ,
.BR sort= ,
.B sidebar=
and
.BR open_in_photo=
(default true).
Set as Wallpaper writes
.B wallpaper=
in
.BR [appearance] .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/sde/gallery/albums/NAME.album
An album: one absolute path per line, in the album's order
.RB ( $XDG_DATA_HOME
is honoured).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sde-view (1),
.BR liria (1),
.BR sde-settings (1),
.BR xdg-user-dir (1),
.BR xdg-email (1)
